# Apps

`apps` is the native local terminal workbench from
[`keys-i/tools`](https://github.com/keys-i/tools). It owns five focused modes:
`read` searches UTF-8 text, `table` parses quoted CSV or TSV, `slides` presents
Markdown pages separated by `---`, `paint` edits a plain-text canvas, and
`timer` runs a monotonic countdown.

The `action` selects `snapshot` or `open`; `app` selects the mode. Supply an
`input` for read, table, or slides, or an optional paint `canvas`. Reader search
uses `--find`; tables accept `--delimiter`; read/table snapshots accept
`--limit`; slides accept `--page`. A new paint canvas accepts `--width` and
`--height`; do not set them with an existing canvas. Interactive paint accepts
`--output` and refuses to replace an existing file. Timers require `--seconds`
and accept snapshot `--elapsed` plus `--label`. Choose the snapshot `format` as
plain text or JSON.

All input is opened once and capped at 32 MiB. Tables stop at 100,000 rows, 256
columns, and two million cells. Paint saves a completed temporary file through
an atomic no-overwrite link. There is no network, TLS, browser, PDF codec,
Wayland compositor, PTY server, plugin, Python process, shell, or upstream
executable.

Keyboard controls are shown in every mode. `q`, Escape, or Ctrl-C exits and the
terminal is restored. This pack contains only the typed UI contract; the
prepared `keys-tools` PyPI package has not been published.
